HAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-model-controller.md:161:| DataScienceCluster CR | CRD Watch | runtime-integration | Read enabled platform components |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-model-controller.md:367:| Component | Interaction Type | Role | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Purpose |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-model-controller.md:394:| DataScienceCluster CR | CRD Watch | runtime-integration |  | HTTPS | TLS 1.2+ | Read enabled platform components |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:1:# Component: kserve\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:16:**Detailed**: KServe provides the core model serving infrastructure for RHOAI, managing inference workloads from single-model deployments through multi-model inference graphs and LLM-optimized serving. The platform is composed of four main controller binaries — the core kserve manager (InferenceService, InferenceGraph, TrainedModel), the LLMInferenceService controller (llmisvc), the local model caching controllers (localmodel/localmodelnode), and the kserve-module operator that manages component installation on OpenShift. Each controller reconciles its CRDs and owns downstream Kubernetes resources (Deployments, Services, HTTPRoutes, PersistentVolumes) through controller-runtime watches. The repository also ships a Python SDK (`kserve` package) with framework-specific model servers (HuggingFace, sklearn, XGBoost, LightGBM, vLLM, and others) that implement the KServe V2 Inference Protocol via both HTTP (FastAPI/uvicorn) and gRPC endpoints. An inference router binary provides authenticated request routing for InferenceGraph DAGs, enforcing access control via Kubernetes TokenReview and SubjectAccessReview APIs. [source: cmd/manager/main.go:288, cmd/llmisvc/main.go:339, cmd/router/main.go:525, kserve-module/cmd/kserve-module/main.go:91, python/kserve/kserve/protocol/grpc/grpc_predict_v2.proto:23]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:22:**Controller topology.** The `manager` binary reconciles the foundational CRDs — InferenceService, InferenceGraph, ClusterServingRuntime, and TrainedModel — creating Deployments, Services, and ingress resources (HTTPRoutes, Istio VirtualServices, or OpenShift Routes depending on platform configuration). The `llmisvc` controller handles the LLMInferenceService and LLMInferenceServiceConfig CRDs with extensive Gateway API integration, managing HorizontalPodAutoscalers, LeaderWorkerSets for multi-node inference, KEDA ScaledObjects, and InferencePool resources for gateway-based load balancing. The `localmodel`/`localmodelnode` pair manages persistent model caching at cluster and node level through PersistentVolume/PersistentVolumeClaim lifecycle and batch Job-based model downloads. The `kserve-module` operator runs from a separate Go module (`kserve-module/`) and manages the installation and configuration of all other KServe components on the ODH/RHOAI platform, watching the `Kserve` CR from `components.platform.opendatahub.io`. [source: pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/controller.go:724, pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/controller.go:419, pkg/controller/v1alpha1/localmodel/reconcilers/localmodelcache_reconciler.go:365, kserve-module/pkg/kservemodule/setup.go:68]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:26:**TLS and platform integration.** The ODH/RHOAI distribution build (`//go:build distro`) includes platform-aware TLS configuration that reads the cluster's TLS security profile from `apiservers.config.openshift.io/cluster` and applies the corresponding cipher suites and minimum TLS version. When the profile is unavailable (non-OpenShift or transient failure), it falls back to Mozilla Intermediate cipher suites with TLS 1.2 minimum. This allows the platform to enforce consistent TLS policy across all KServe controller endpoints without per-component configuration. [source: pkg/tls/tls_odh.go:73-100]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:47:## Architecture Components\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:49:| Component | Type | Purpose |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:115:| components.platform.opendatahub.io | v1alpha1 | Kserve | Cluster | Core API | Custom resource managed by kserve |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:199:| Component | Version | Required | Role | Purpose |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:251:| k8s.io/component-helpers | v0.35.3 | Yes |  | Go module dependency |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:379:| Component | Interaction Type | Role | Purpose |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-wfar2syk/.context/a