ng the agreed p50/p95 scale-from-zero targets once available.\n- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments, incorporating Performance/PSAP team input.\n- Supported configuration matrix across both paths and topologies; troubleshooting for misconfigured triggers and failed zero-to-one transitions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Documentation covers both autoscaling paths and static allocation with a decision guide, per-workload-shape configuration recipes, troubleshooting, and a supported configuration matrix.\n- The standalone KEDA instructions include referencing the TriggerAuthentication resource for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift, and KEDA installation as a prerequisite with GitOps-referenced guidance.\n- Recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics are documented, with example ScaledObject templates.\n- Scale-from-zero latency expectations, headroom recommendations, and fleet-scale Prometheus capacity guidance are included, reflecting the inputs received from the owning teams for those open questions; where an input is still pending, best-available values are documented and explicitly flagged as pending.\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of both autoscaling paths and validated against the architecture context (kserve, odh-model-controller, and workload-variant-autoscaler architecture context files).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 [P1]: well-lit path documentation covering both autoscaling paths with decision guide, configuration recipes per workload shape, and troubleshooting.\n- HLR-3 [P0]: scale-to-zero — configuration guidance for KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0`.\n- HLR-4 [P0]: scale-from-zero — recommended trigger configurations using EPP queue metrics and example templates.\n- HLR-5 [P0]: disaggregated prefill/decode independent scaling — per-workload-shape recipes.\n- HLR-6 [P1]: operator guidance for observing scaling events with signa