open question gating the OpenShift delivery of HLR-1.\n70\t\n71\tAll seven HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n72\t\n73\t## Unknowns Disposition (Step 3)\n74\t\n75\t| Unknown (source) | Changes which epics exist / what they do? | Disposition |\n76\t|------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------|\n77\t| Open Question 1: downstream adaptation beyond authentication context (RBAC/TLS) — owner: KServe team | YES — changes what the odh-model-controller epic must build | Investigation epic E001, gating E003 (`add_remediation`) |\n78\t| Open Question 2: target p50/p95 for scale-from-zero — owner: llm-d team | NO — determines headroom/cold-start recommendations (documentation content), not epic structure | Acceptance criterion / content input on E004; health warning on cross-team input timing |\n79\t| Open Question 3: Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet scale — owner: Performance/PSAP team | NO — documentation content only | Acceptance criterion / content input on E004; health warning on cross-team input timing |\n80\t| Assumption: KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` pauses/resumes correctly for LLM workloads (\"needs validation\") | NO — implementation proceeds the same way; failure = fix-and-retry | Integration-test acceptance criterion on E002 (scale-to-zero / scale-from-zero round trip) |\n81\t| Assumption: EPP flow control queue metrics available at zero replicas (\"needs validation\") | NO — trigger configuration is user-defined either way; failure changes docs guidance, not epic structure | Acceptance criterion on E002 integration testing; risk carried on E004 (recommended trigger configurations, example templates) |\n82\t| Assumption: PR kserve/kserve#5839 lands upstream (\"needs validation\") | Timing risk, not structural — fallback (carry patch downstream with backport) is an acceptance criterion on E002, per Rule 21 (viable fallback → AC, not separate epic) | Tiered delivery (below) |\n83\t\n84\t## Component Name Mappings\n85\t\n86\tCanonical component values (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) for strategy components that have no verbatim canonical name:\n87\t\n88\t| Strategy component | Canonical value | Rationale |\n89\t|--------------------|-----------------|-----------|\n90\t| KServe (llmisvc-controller) | `Serving Orchestration` | KServe is the model-serving orchestration layer; no canonical \"KServe\" component exists. |\n91\t| odh-model-controller | `INFERENG Midstream` | odh-model-controller originates in the opendatahub-io midstream and implements inference-engineering (model serving) reconciliation; no verbatim canonical name exists. |\n92\t| Documentation | `Documentation` | Verbatim match. |\n93\t\n94\t## Health Warnings\n95\t\n96\t- **Docs epic priority vs. HLR priority**: E004 is P0 because the docs-authoring exception derives priority from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Critical`), even though the documentation HLR-7 is P1. Flagged for human verification at review.\n97\t- **Cross-team content inputs**: two open questions owned by other teams (llm-d: scale-from-zero p50/p95 target; Performance/PSAP: fleet-scale Prometheus capacity guidance) feed E004's content. Their timing is not controlled by this pipeline; E004 carries an AC to document best-available values and flag pending input rather than block.\n98\t- **Upstream PR timing**: kserve/kserve#5839 is open and in progress. If acceptance is delayed, E002's fallback (carry the patch downstream via the midstream fork with a backport plan) keeps the timeline bounded but shifts integration risk downstream. Noted as an AC on E002 and a risk on E002.\n99\t- **Strategy-level process gates**: Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and other Prerequisites are all \"Pending human review\" placeholders in the strategy. This decomposition assumes they resolve without changing scope; license validation is not generated as an epic because both affected components already exist in the platform with no new extern