{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a35b104c724b492","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n3\ttitle: Standalone KEDA autoscaling path in the KServe llmisvc-controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Serving Orchestration\n6\tteam: Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standalone KEDA autoscaling path in the KServe llmisvc-controller\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tImplement standalone KEDA autoscaling as a first-class path for LLMInferenceService in the KServe llmisvc-controller, following the accepted upstream design (kserve/kserve#5646) and its implementation PR (kserve/kserve#5839): users configure KEDA triggers directly in the LLMInferenceService spec without deploying WVA, bringing parity with v1beta1 InferenceService. This covers the API types, CEL validation, controller branching, scaling status conditions, and landing the change upstream (or carrying it downstream as fallback).\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- API type changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_types.go`: standalone KEDA spec at the ScalingSpec level with `pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`, and a `triggers` field for user-defined KEDA trigger definitions (type, metadata map).\n38\t- Validation changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_validation.go`: relax the CEL rule from requiring `wva` to requiring at least one of `wva` or `keda`, enforce mutual exclusivity between the two paths, validate trigger completeness, and keep `spec.scaling` mutually exclusive with static `spec.replicas`.\n39\t- For disaggregated deployments, enforce that prefill and decode phases use the same scaling path, preserving actuator consistency (architecture overlay 0011).\n40\t- Controller changes in `pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/scaling.go`: branch on the configured path — the standalone KEDA path creates a ScaledObject from user-provided triggers (Resource, External, and PodMetric trigger types, per the v1beta1 reference reconciler at `pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/reconcilers/keda/keda_reconciler.go`) and skips VariantAutoscaling CR creation entirely.\n41\t- Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` and scale-from-zero via user-configured triggers (e.g. Prometheus queries on EPP flow control queue metrics); phase-specific ScaledObjects for independent prefill/decode scaling in disaggregated deployments.\n42\t- Scaling status conditions for both paths and KEDA ScaledObject event emission with signal attribution for the standalone path.\n43\t- Regression safety: existing WVA-mediated autoscaling and static deployments (no `spec.scaling`) behave identically to before; the standalone KEDA path is additive.\n44\t- Landing: drive the change to merge in upstream kserve (PR kserve/kserve#5839 or successor); if upstream acceptance is delayed, carry the patch via the midstream/downstream fork with a backport plan once merged.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` configured with user-defined triggers and no WVA deployed, when a trigger condition is met (e.g. a Prometheus query threshold is exceeded), then the deployment scales up — measured by KEDA ScaledObject status showing active and Deployment replica count increasing.\n49\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with both `spec.scaling.wva` and `spec.scaling.keda` set, when the CR is submitted, then the API server rejects it with a CEL validation error indicating mutual exclusivity.\n50\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` and no `spec.scaling.wva`, when the llmisvc-controller reconciles, then no VariantAutoscaling CR is created and a ScaledObject with the user-provided triggers is created — measured by `kubectl get variantautoscalings` returning empty and `kubectl get scaledobjects` returning a ScaledObject with the user's triggers.\n51\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with KEDA and `idleReplicaCount: 0`, when no requests are received for the cooldown period, then the deployment scales to zero — measured by Deployment replica count reaching 0 and KEDA ScaledObject status showing idle — and a subsequent trigger condition scales it back up from zero to serving (this round trip validates the scale-from-zero assumption for LLM inference workloads).\n52\t- Given a disaggregated LLMInferenceService with separate scaling configs, when prefill pods reach saturation while decode pods remain below threshold, then only the prefill pool scales up — measured by independent scaling resource status for prefill and decode roles — and a CR configuring different scaling paths for the two phases is rejected by validation.\n53\t- Given a deployment with autoscaling active, when Prometheus metrics become unavailable, then the deployment holds its current replica count — measured by replica count remaining stable during the metric outage.\n54\t- Static deployments with no autoscaling configured continue to serve identically — measured by no VariantAutoscaling, HPA, or ScaledObject resources created for deployments without `spec.scaling`, and by the existing WVA-path test suite passing unchanged.\n55\t- Scaling events for the standalone path are emitted as KEDA ScaledObject events with signal attribution.\n56\t- The standalone KEDA support is landed in upstream kserve, or carried in the midstream/downstream fork with a documented backport plan (fallback if upstream acceptance is delayed).\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-1 [P0]: LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment — API, validation, and controller implementation.\n61\t- HLR-2 [P0]: the two autoscaling paths are mutually exclusive at the API level with CEL validation enforcing at-least-one and at-most-one.\n62\t- HLR-3 [P0]: scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths).\n63\t- HLR-4 [P0]: scale-from-zero — standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers (the WVA path's dedicated engine already exists).\n64\t- HLR-5 [P0]: disaggregated prefill and decode pools scale independently based on their respective load profiles.\n65\t- HLR-6 [P1]: scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution (KEDA ScaledObject events for the standalone path) — bundled with the P0 work because event emission falls out of the same ScaledObject creation surface.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83d800cd5acabd92","agent_id":"aecb55fe7396d6010","session_id":"04280142-99a3-46b0-81af-b1932074d3a4","uuid":"fcf343ae-e523-462e-bee5-b43b99ccaed4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:16:28.297Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a35b104c724b492","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
